{
  "annotations": {
    "list": []
  },
  "editable": true,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "title": "Warehouse \u2014 API Gateway (Kong) overview",
  "uid": "warehouse-kong-gateway-overview",
  "tags": [
    "warehouse",
    "kong",
    "gateway"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-30m",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "refresh": "30s",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Kong Gateway health",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Datastore reachable",
      "description": "kong_datastore_reachable. This chart runs Kong DB-less (env.database=off, see kong.tf), so this reflects Kong's own config-loading health, not an external Postgres/Cassandra dependency.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "kong_datastore_reachable",
          "legendFormat": "{{pod}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Nginx metric/connection errors",
      "description": "kong_nginx_metric_errors_total -- errors internal to Kong's own metrics collection (not request errors). Should stay at zero.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(kong_nginx_metric_errors_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "errors/sec"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Upstream target health",
      "description": "kong_upstream_target_health: 1 = healthy, per upstream/target. A target stuck at 0 for a Service backing a bounded context's Deployment means Kong has marked every replica of that pod unreachable.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "kong_upstream_target_health",
          "legendFormat": "{{upstream}} {{target}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Traffic by bounded context",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 9
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Request rate by context",
      "description": "Requests/sec Kong is forwarding, summed by the Kong Service name (one per bounded context's route -- see locals.tf's `services` map / Gateway API HTTPRoute-derived Service naming, httproute.warehouse-systems.<context>.0).",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 10
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (service) (rate(kong_http_requests_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{service}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "5xx error rate by context",
      "description": "5xx responses per bounded context's Kong Service, so one failing context is visible without averaging across the fleet.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 10
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (service) (rate(kong_http_requests_total{code=~\"5..\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{service}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Latency",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 19
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Upstream latency p95 by context",
      "description": "Time Kong spent waiting on each context's own pod (excludes Kong's own processing overhead) -- the fairest cross-context latency comparison since it isolates the application, not the gateway.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 20
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ms"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (service, le) (rate(kong_upstream_latency_ms_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{service}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Kong-added overhead p95 by context",
      "description": "kong_kong_latency_ms: time Kong itself spends on the request (routing, plugins -- CORS, this Prometheus exporter) excluding the upstream call. A rise here fleet-wide, uncorrelated with any single context, points at the gateway (e.g. plugin config), not a bounded context.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 20
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ms"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (service, le) (rate(kong_kong_latency_ms_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{service}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Bandwidth",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 29
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Bandwidth by context and direction",
      "description": "kong_bandwidth_bytes, ingress (client->Kong) vs. egress (Kong->client), by context. Useful for spotting a context whose responses have ballooned in size (e.g. an unpaginated list endpoint).",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 30
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "Bps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (service, direction) (rate(kong_bandwidth_bytes[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{service}} {{direction}}"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
